{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'screen|reader|allow-list|page' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | head -45; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11830,11838p'\"","aggregated_output":"8:Opening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\n11:could reach a reader:\n15:- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\n19:A rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\n20:stop answering findings: propose one structural rule\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\n33:## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\n36:  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\n38:  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\n40:- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\n46:  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\n47:- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\n63:- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\n92:allow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\n94:  readers would see.\n99:  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\n105:  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\n118:- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\n120:  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\n134:  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n 11830\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n 11831\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11832\t  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\n 11833\t  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n 11834\t    forecast text and the history withheld together.\n 11835\t  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n 11836\t    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\" appear.\n 11837\t- **Kept for the record, not built:**\n 11838\t  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
